# Normalize line endings.
#
# Development happens on Windows and CI runs on Linux. Without this, every file
# committed from Windows carries CRLF into the repository, and diffs fill with
# whole-file changes that hide the real ones. Storing LF in the repository and
# letting Git check out the platform's native ending keeps both sides happy.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must keep LF even when checked out on Windows - CRLF breaks the
# shebang line on Linux.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary files Git must never try to normalize.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
